  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The World Athletics Federation is the governing body overseeing the World Athletics Championship and record validations.&lt;SEP&gt;The World Athletics Federation is the governing body overseeing the World Athletics Championship and record validations.&lt;SEP&gt;The World Athletics Federation is the governing body overseeing the World Athletics Championship and record validations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfaea66e0e1b59fcf11083fdc86fa505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-288c1ac0daa4f8d9e6711072456bf290&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4041840a72080e115133366da601ba0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9666bb1f91905773a4411559f12b0410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3968d482efd321ce0e71494d6d8cbde6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697366b5ec6fccd401f60e32f476bcb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-764b1321ae6bc951a2c8d2de5901567f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medication overuse headache">
  <data key="d0">Medication overuse headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Medication overuse headache is a condition that can develop from overuse of migraine medications, requiring weaning to monitor for withdrawal symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfaea66e0e1b59fcf11083fdc86fa505</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711454</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dystonic reactions">
  <data key="d0">Dystonic reactions</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Dystonic reactions are muscle contractions causing abnormal postures, which can be induced as a side effect of certain medications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfaea66e0e1b59fcf11083fdc86fa505</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711454</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ischemic vascular disease">
  <data key="d0">Ischemic vascular disease</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ischemic vascular disease involving cardiac, cerebrovascular, or peripheral circulations is a contraindication for the use of dihydroergotamine.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfaea66e0e1b59fcf11083fdc86fa505</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711454</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Early headache recurrence">
  <data key="d0">Early headache recurrence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Early headache recurrence is the risk of migraine returning after initial treatment, which can be reduced with adjunctive dexamethasone.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfaea66e0e1b59fcf11083fdc86fa505</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711454</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nonopioid medications">
  <data key="d0">Nonopioid medications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nonopioid medications are recommended as first-line therapy for severe migraine according to practice guidelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfaea66e0e1b59fcf11083fdc86fa505</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711454</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Opioid medications">
  <data key="d0">Opioid medications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Opioid medications are noted for widespread overuse in emergency departments for acute headache, despite guidelines recommending nonopioid alternatives.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfaea66e0e1b59fcf11083fdc86fa505</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711454</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zavegepant">
  <data key="d0">Zavegepant</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Zavegepant is given at 10 mg intranasally as a single spray and was approved for acute migraine by the US FDA in 2023.&lt;SEP&gt;Zavegepant is a nasal spray formulation used for the acute treatment of migraine.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-81f90692986dfb1f830a27d0b7536f61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c43e57d7c9eb41cc91c89593e5618e6</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711454</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serotonin 1F Receptor">
  <data key="d0">Serotonin 1F Receptor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The serotonin 1F receptor is the target of lasmiditan for migraine treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-81f90692986dfb1f830a27d0b7536f61</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711454</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ergotamine">
  <data key="d0">Ergotamine</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Ergotamine is a medication primarily utilized for the acute and preventive treatment of migraine and cluster headaches. It functions by binding to 5HT1b/d receptors, and is available in various formulations such as oral tablets, rectal suppositories, and sublingual tablets. While effective for abortive migraine treatment and cluster headache attacks since the 1940s, its use is accompanied by significant safety considerations. It is contraindicated during pregnancy due to the risk of inducing uterine contractions and vasoconstriction, and must not be administered to patients who have taken a triptan within the preceding 24 hours. Additionally, it is sometimes combined with caffeine in rectal suppository form to prevent nighttime cluster headaches. In specific contexts, it can be used safely alongside verapamil for prevention. However, its use is limited by a risk of side effects and complications, necessitating careful patient selection and dosing, such as a maximum of 6 mg daily and 10 mg weekly for cluster headache management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-81f90692986dfb1f830a27d0b7536f61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81fbead48486691cf5945207e3542587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-288c1ac0daa4f8d9e6711072456bf290&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-075c9514b73c9528ed6f8491b449ee40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697366b5ec6fccd401f60e32f476bcb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e431a39c5b3ac9ad50817fd6694435f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f74beccf3932fc999c5da6217dd983e</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Migraine Prevention">
  <data key="d0">Migraine Prevention</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Migraine prevention refers to the prophylactic use of medications to reduce the frequency and severity of migraine attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Migraine prevention is reviewed separately in the context of neuromodulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Migraine prevention involves strategies and medications to reduce the frequency of migraine attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-81f90692986dfb1f830a27d0b7536f61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c43e57d7c9eb41cc91c89593e5618e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c97fa32b2d7b605eb00ea730f0821e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d38115148b4b0478b2ff0c5f850bbcb7</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711454</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acute Migraine Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Acute Migraine Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acute migraine treatment refers to the use of medications to stop a migraine attack in progress.&lt;SEP&gt;Acute migraine treatment refers to the medical management of migraine attacks at their onset.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-81f90692986dfb1f830a27d0b7536f61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711454</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pain">
  <data key="d0">Pain</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Pain is the primary symptom of migraine, often described as throbbing or pulsating headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Pain is a medical journal publishing research on pain management.&lt;SEP&gt;Pain is a primary symptom of migraine, being the focus of acute treatment outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-81f90692986dfb1f830a27d0b7536f61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c43e57d7c9eb41cc91c89593e5618e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27dde5a0572eb3184020966c72e61c89</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711454</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Triptans">
  <data key="d0">Triptans</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Triptans are a class of migraine-specific agents used for the acute treatment of moderate to severe migraine attacks. These medications are considered safe and effective for most patients; however, their use should be limited to no more than 10 days per month to avoid the risk of medication overuse headache. Clinically, triptans are employed as first-line therapy for severe migraine attacks or those that respond poorly to NSAIDs. Pharmacologically, they function by inhibiting transmission in the trigeminal nucleus caudalis and blocking afferent input to second-order neurons. Available formulations include subcutaneous sumatriptan, nasal sumatriptan, and zolmitriptan. Importantly, triptans should not be used within 24 hours of ergotamine administration. The class is extensively reviewed in the literature for its comparative pharmacology, pharmacokinetics, and efficacy in the symptomatic treatment of migraine headaches.&lt;SEP&gt;Triptans are a class of medications generally well tolerated but include side effects such as nonischemic chest pain and distal paresthesia, and are recommended to be administered as soon as the headache begins for more effective treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Triptans are an effective alternative initial treatment option for acute cluster headache attacks, particularly subcutaneous sumatriptan.&lt;SEP&gt;Triptans such as sumatriptan or zolmitriptan are recommended as initial acute therapy for cluster headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Triptans include oral naratriptan and frovatriptan, which have limited data suggesting benefit for cluster headache prevention, while oral sumatriptan was found not effective for preventing attacks in a multicenter placebo-controlled trial of 169 patients. Ergotamine combined with caffeine is advocated as a rectal suppository to prevent nighttime attacks, though ergotamine alone is not available as a suppository.&lt;SEP&gt;Triptans are a reasonable alternative when oxygen is not effective or readily available and may be more convenient for some patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Triptans are a reasonable alternative treatment for acute cluster headache when oxygen is not effective or readily available.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfaea66e0e1b59fcf11083fdc86fa505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b20a73b1bf34e686ee6652ff377b531a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-288c1ac0daa4f8d9e6711072456bf290&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9781a20ce9291545e13c64cc40854f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c97fa32b2d7b605eb00ea730f0821e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4041840a72080e115133366da601ba0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eced74bbae68c4d04d0938805d606b4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4bdd16b737b7973c6581c7cc92604b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27dde5a0572eb3184020966c72e61c89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d38115148b4b0478b2ff0c5f850bbcb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-075c9514b73c9528ed6f8491b449ee40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697366b5ec6fccd401f60e32f476bcb8</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acetaminophen">
  <data key="d0">Acetaminophen</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Acetaminophen is a simple analgesic used for mild migraine attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetaminophen is an effective abortive agent in some patients and can be combined with NSAIDs and/or caffeine to enhance effect.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetaminophen is a pain reliever that may be used with rizatriptan.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetaminophen (paracetamol) is evaluated for acute migraine headaches, often in combination with an antiemetic or caffeine, in randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trials.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetaminophen is a nonopioid analgesic suggested for mild migraine attacks without vomiting or severe nausea.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetaminophen is a medication compared with rizatriptan for acute migraine treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;If acetaminophen has not already been taken by the patient, it is reasonable to give a full dose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9781a20ce9291545e13c64cc40854f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eced74bbae68c4d04d0938805d606b4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4bdd16b737b7973c6581c7cc92604b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5254cc12db8ae366992b8abc63e9bce0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36b9bf57cb93bcd7302da2d7f4b4041b</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711759</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Noninvasive Neuromodulation Devices">
  <data key="d0">Noninvasive Neuromodulation Devices</data>
  <data key="d1">device</data>
  <data key="d2">Noninvasive neuromodulation devices are typically used for patients who do not respond to or tolerate drug treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711454</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Algorithm 1">
  <data key="d0">Algorithm 1</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Algorithm 1 is a treatment strategy for acute migraine in adults comparing step care and stratified care approaches.&lt;SEP&gt;Algorithm 1 guides the selection of prophylactic pharmacotherapy based on symptom severity, comorbid conditions, and prior treatment response.&lt;SEP&gt;Algorithm 1 refers to the suggested initial treatment protocol for acute cluster headache attacks involving oxygen inhalation.&lt;SEP&gt;Algorithm 1 is a clinical tool used by emergency clinicians to identify patients with life-threatening headaches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eced74bbae68c4d04d0938805d606b4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mild Migraine Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Mild Migraine Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mild migraine attacks are typically treated with simple analgesics or combination analgesics as first-line therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711454</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Moderate to Severe Migraine Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Moderate to Severe Migraine Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Moderate to severe migraine attacks require first-line oral options including triptans with or without NSAIDs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eced74bbae68c4d04d0938805d606b4f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711454</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medication Overuse Headache">
  <data key="d0">Medication Overuse Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Medication overuse headache is a risk associated with frequent use of acute migraine medications.&lt;SEP&gt;Medication overuse headache is a risk associated with opioid and butalbital use.&lt;SEP&gt;Medication overuse headache is a concern with recurrent use of triptans, recommending subcutaneous sumatriptan 6 mg limited to no more than two doses in 24 hours and intranasal sumatriptan 20 mg to no more than two doses (40 mg) in 24 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22a7faa6dc2428acdd3ea3c1593916bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b20a73b1bf34e686ee6652ff377b531a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccbcc20d04c05bb1a254eb147d0d3a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Randomized Controlled Trial">
  <data key="d0">Randomized Controlled Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A randomized controlled trial of 835 adults with migraine compared treatment strategies for acute migraine.&lt;SEP&gt;Randomized Controlled Trial is a study design that randomly assigns participants to treatment or control groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Randomized controlled trial is a study design used to evaluate the efficacy and safety of migraine treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c43e57d7c9eb41cc91c89593e5618e6</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711454</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Step Care Within Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Step Care Within Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Step care within attacks involves initial treatment with aspirin plus metoclopramide, escalating to zolmitriptan if no response after two hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Step Care Across Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Step Care Across Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Step care across attacks involves initial treatment with aspirin plus metoclopramide; non-responders switch to zolmitriptan for subsequent attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stratified Care">
  <data key="d0">Stratified Care</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Stratified care involves treating mild headaches with aspirin plus metoclopramide and severe headaches with zolmitriptan.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vascular Risk Factors">
  <data key="d0">Vascular Risk Factors</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Vascular risk factors are patient-specific considerations influencing the pharmacologic approach to migraine treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Drug Preference">
  <data key="d0">Drug Preference</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Drug preference is a patient-specific factor influencing migraine treatment selection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Naproxen">
  <data key="d0">Naproxen</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Naproxen is a medication evaluated for acute migraine headaches in adults, commonly studied with or without an antiemetic in Cochrane reviews.&lt;SEP&gt;Naproxen is an NSAID used for treating acute migraine.&lt;SEP&gt;Naproxen is a medication used in combination with sumatriptan for the treatment of acute migraine attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4bdd16b737b7973c6581c7cc92604b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5254cc12db8ae366992b8abc63e9bce0</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rizatriptan">
  <data key="d0">Rizatriptan</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Rizatriptan is an oral triptan whose dose must be adjusted downward in patients taking propranolol, as propranolol increases rizatriptan levels by 70 percent.&lt;SEP&gt;Rizatriptan is a triptan medication demonstrated effective for acute migraine in systematic reviews of placebo-controlled studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Rizatriptan is a triptan that may be coadministered with NSAIDs.&lt;SEP&gt;Rizatriptan is a medication used for acute migraine treatment, often compared with acetaminophen in studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4041840a72080e115133366da601ba0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f034fb31d8b9231647be0271fbbe11ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5254cc12db8ae366992b8abc63e9bce0</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frovatriptan">
  <data key="d0">Frovatriptan</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Frovatriptan is a triptan with a slower onset of action and may have the lowest propensity to cause side effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Frovatriptan is one of the available triptan preparations for acute migraine treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Frovatriptan is a triptan that may be coadministered with NSAIDs.&lt;SEP&gt;Frovatriptan is a triptan medication used in combination with dexketoprofen for migraine treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Frovatriptan is a longer-acting triptan with limited data suggesting benefit for cluster headache prevention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4041840a72080e115133366da601ba0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f034fb31d8b9231647be0271fbbe11ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5254cc12db8ae366992b8abc63e9bce0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-075c9514b73c9528ed6f8491b449ee40</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dexketoprofen">
  <data key="d0">Dexketoprofen</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Dexketoprofen is an NSAID that may be combined with frovatriptan.&lt;SEP&gt;Dexketoprofen trometamol was studied in a phase II randomized, double-blind, crossover, placebo-controlled dose optimization study for acute migraine treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Dexketoprofen is an anti-inflammatory medication combined with frovatriptan for migraine treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4bdd16b737b7973c6581c7cc92604b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5254cc12db8ae366992b8abc63e9bce0</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Meloxicam">
  <data key="d0">Meloxicam</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Meloxicam is an NSAID that may be combined with rizatriptan.&lt;SEP&gt;Meloxicam is a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) used in combination with rizatriptan.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5254cc12db8ae366992b8abc63e9bce0</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydromorphone">
  <data key="d0">Hydromorphone</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydromorphone is an opioid medication compared with prochlorperazine and diphenhydramine for migraine treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5254cc12db8ae366992b8abc63e9bce0</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Droperidol">
  <data key="d0">Droperidol</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Droperidol is a medication administered parenterally (IV or IM), found to be superior to placebo for acute migraine relief.&lt;SEP&gt;Droperidol is a medication compared with metoclopramide for acute migraine therapy in the emergency department.&lt;SEP&gt;Droperidol is used to treat undifferentiated headache in the ED.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3968d482efd321ce0e71494d6d8cbde6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-764b1321ae6bc951a2c8d2de5901567f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ondansetron">
  <data key="d0">Ondansetron</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Ondansetron is a medication used for migraine treatment, though associated with a high incidence of headache as an adverse effect.&lt;SEP&gt;Ondansetron is a medication known to induce headache in some patients, particularly in gynecological cancer and parturient settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Ondansetron is a parenteral agent used to treat nausea and vomiting, making patients more comfortable during diagnostic and therapeutic steps.&lt;SEP&gt;Treating nausea and vomiting with a parenteral agent such as ondansetron may make the patient more comfortable while other diagnostic and therapeutic steps are occurring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3968d482efd321ce0e71494d6d8cbde6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-764b1321ae6bc951a2c8d2de5901567f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36b9bf57cb93bcd7302da2d7f4b4041b</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cochrane Database">
  <data key="d0">Cochrane Database</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Cochrane Database Syst Rev is a repository of systematic reviews, including reviews on migraine treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JAMA">
  <data key="d0">JAMA</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">JAMA is a medical journal publishing clinical trials and research on migraine treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NEJM">
  <data key="d0">NEJM</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">New England Journal of Medicine publishing significant clinical trials on migraine treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FDA">
  <data key="d0">FDA</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">FDA (Food and Drug Administration) is the regulatory body that approves new treatments for migraine.&lt;SEP&gt;FDA (Food and Drug Administration) regulates drug labels and approvals, including meloxicam-rizatriptan.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c43e57d7c9eb41cc91c89593e5618e6</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ClinicalTrials.gov">
  <data key="d0">ClinicalTrials.gov</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">ClinicalTrials.gov is a registry of clinical studies, including the MOMENTUM trial (NCT03896009).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Migraine with Aura">
  <data key="d0">Migraine with Aura</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Migraine with aura is a subtype of episodic migraine tested in the transcranial magnetic stimulation trial.&lt;SEP&gt;Migraine with aura is a subtype of migraine attacks characterized by sensory disturbances preceding the headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c97fa32b2d7b605eb00ea730f0821e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74803e1d9bd621760a74773f08649443</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Migraine without Aura">
  <data key="d0">Migraine without Aura</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Migraine without aura is the most common subtype of migraine attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gynecological Cancer">
  <data key="d0">Gynecological Cancer</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Gynecological cancer is a clinical setting where ondansetron-induced headache has been observed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Parturient">
  <data key="d0">Parturient</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Parturient refers to a woman in labor, a setting where ondansetron-induced headache has been mimicking postdural puncture headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Migraine Type Headache">
  <data key="d0">Migraine Type Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Migraine-type headache is a specific headache phenotype induced by medications like ondansetron.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Migraine Treatment Comparison">
  <data key="d0">Migraine Treatment Comparison</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Migraine treatment comparison involves randomized trials evaluating different drug combinations and routes of administration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Systematic Review">
  <data key="d0">Systematic Review</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Systematic review is a method used to summarize evidence from multiple studies on a specific topic.&lt;SEP&gt;Systematic review is a method used to synthesize evidence on pharmacologic therapies for migraine in the emergency department.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27dde5a0572eb3184020966c72e61c89</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bayesian Network Meta-analysis">
  <data key="d0">Bayesian Network Meta-analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bayesian network meta-analysis is a statistical method used to compare multiple treatments simultaneously.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Placebo-Controlled Trial">
  <data key="d0">Placebo-Controlled Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A randomized placebo-controlled trial evaluated 403 patients with migraine to assess almotriptan efficacy.&lt;SEP&gt;Placebo-controlled trial is a study design using a placebo group to assess treatment efficacy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b20a73b1bf34e686ee6652ff377b531a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df12cd945c38984efea15b2addfde26f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intravenous Administration">
  <data key="d0">Intravenous Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intravenous administration is a method of delivering dihydroergotamine, typically requiring combination with an antiemetic.&lt;SEP&gt;Intravenous administration is a route of drug delivery studied for acute migraine therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81fbead48486691cf5945207e3542587</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711455</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subcutaneous Administration">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Subcutaneous administration is a method of delivering dihydroergotamine, often compared with sumatriptan in clinical trials.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous administration is a route of drug delivery compared with intravenous administration for migraine therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous administration involves injection in areas with adequate skin and subcutaneous thickness, and the injection site should be rotated to reduce the risk of local reactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81fbead48486691cf5945207e3542587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oral Administration">
  <data key="d0">Oral Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Oral administration is a route for several triptans including rizatriptan, sumatriptan, and naratriptan.&lt;SEP&gt;Oral administration is a route of drug delivery studied for migraine treatment efficacy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4041840a72080e115133366da601ba0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df12cd945c38984efea15b2addfde26f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gynecological Setting">
  <data key="d0">Gynecological Setting</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Gynecological setting is a clinical environment where ondansetron-induced headache has been observed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Postdural Puncture Headache">
  <data key="d0">Postdural Puncture Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Postdural puncture headache is a headache type that ondansetron-induced headache has been reported to mimic.&lt;SEP&gt;Postdural puncture headache (if the patient had a spinal anesthetic) or spontaneous intracranial hypotension (in patients without a spinal anesthetic) due to dural tears sustained during labor-related pushing.&lt;SEP&gt;Postdural puncture headache can occur after spinal anesthetic, worsening upon standing postpartum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88449f41c18acfddbc679b10a20feb42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccbcc20d04c05bb1a254eb147d0d3a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711755</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sumatriptan-Naproxen Combination">
  <data key="d0">Sumatriptan-Naproxen Combination</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sumatriptan-naproxen combination is a fixed-dose combination medication used for the acute treatment of migraine attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rizatriptan-Acetaminophen Combination">
  <data key="d0">Rizatriptan-Acetaminophen Combination</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rizatriptan-acetaminophen combination is a treatment regimen evaluated for acute migraine management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frovatriptan-Dexketoprofen Combination">
  <data key="d0">Frovatriptan-Dexketoprofen Combination</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Frovatriptan-dexketoprofen combination is a treatment regimen for migraine attacks with or without aura.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Meloxicam-Rizatriptan Fixed Dose">
  <data key="d0">Meloxicam-Rizatriptan Fixed Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Meloxicam-rizatriptan is a fixed-dose combination product for acute migraine treatment, available as a specific medication formulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intravenous Prochlorperazine">
  <data key="d0">Intravenous Prochlorperazine</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Intravenous prochlorperazine is an antiemetic medication administered via the intravenous route for acute migraine treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5254cc12db8ae366992b8abc63e9bce0</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intravenous Hydromorphone">
  <data key="d0">Intravenous Hydromorphone</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Intravenous hydromorphone is an opioid medication administered via the intravenous route for migraine treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intravenous Metoclopramide">
  <data key="d0">Intravenous Metoclopramide</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Intravenous metoclopramide is used as a preceding treatment in emergency department settings for migraine.&lt;SEP&gt;Intravenous metoclopramide is an antiemetic medication administered via the intravenous route for acute migraine therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22a7faa6dc2428acdd3ea3c1593916bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5254cc12db8ae366992b8abc63e9bce0</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subcutaneous Sumatriptan">
  <data key="d0">Subcutaneous Sumatriptan</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Subcutaneous sumatriptan is a formulation with the fastest onset of action for acute migraine, typically administered at an initial dose of 6 mg, which may be repeated once after one hour if needed.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous Sumatriptan is a triptan administered via injection, used for migraine pain relief.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous sumatriptan is a triptan medication administered via the subcutaneous route for acute migraine therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous sumatriptan is administered by injection in areas with adequate skin and subcutaneous thickness, such as the abdomen, thighs, and upper arms, with a 3 mg dose effective for some patients and a maximum single dose of 6 mg.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f034fb31d8b9231647be0271fbbe11ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3968d482efd321ce0e71494d6d8cbde6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5254cc12db8ae366992b8abc63e9bce0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ondansetron-Induced Headache">
  <data key="d0">Ondansetron-Induced Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ondansetron-induced headache is a recognized adverse effect of ondansetron, observed in gynecological cancer patients and parturients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Postdural Puncture Headache Mimic">
  <data key="d0">Postdural Puncture Headache Mimic</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ondansetron-induced headache can mimic postdural puncture headache, particularly in parturient settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ca64ee464064b0ec87b1acd587b7d970</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eletriptan">
  <data key="d0">Eletriptan</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Eletriptan is primarily metabolized by cytochrome P-450 enzyme CYP3A4 and should not be used within 72 hours of potent CYP3A4 inhibitors.&lt;SEP&gt;Eletriptan is an oral triptan noted for having the highest likelihood of consistent success and being the most likely to produce short-term and sustained benefit.&lt;SEP&gt;Eletriptan is a triptan medication available in doses of 20, 40, and 80 mg, with efficacy dependent on dose.&lt;SEP&gt;Eletriptan is a triptan medication used for acute migraine treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b20a73b1bf34e686ee6652ff377b531a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4041840a72080e115133366da601ba0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f034fb31d8b9231647be0271fbbe11ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27dde5a0572eb3184020966c72e61c89</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Database Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Database Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Another study analyzed a database of 130,000 migraine attacks in 28,000 patients with migraine.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b20a73b1bf34e686ee6652ff377b531a</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Danish Case-Crossover Study">
  <data key="d0">Danish Case-Crossover Study</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A Danish case-crossover study of more than 429,000 individuals assessed triptan risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b20a73b1bf34e686ee6652ff377b531a</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Migraine Subtypes">
  <data key="d0">Migraine Subtypes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Migraine subtypes include hemiplegic migraine and migraine with brainstem aura, where triptans are avoided due to theoretical risk of cerebral vasoconstriction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b20a73b1bf34e686ee6652ff377b531a</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serotonin Syndrome Risk">
  <data key="d0">Serotonin Syndrome Risk</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Risk of serotonin syndrome when triptans are combined with SSRIs or SNRIs, though the added risk appears very low to nonexistent.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b20a73b1bf34e686ee6652ff377b531a</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Drug Interaction Contraindications">
  <data key="d0">Drug Interaction Contraindications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Triptans should not be used within 24 hours of ergotamine preparations or a different triptan medication; combination with monoamine oxidase inhibitors is relatively contraindicated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b20a73b1bf34e686ee6652ff377b531a</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CYP3A4 Metabolism">
  <data key="d0">CYP3A4 Metabolism</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Eletriptan is primarily metabolized by cytochrome P-450 enzyme CYP3A4.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b20a73b1bf34e686ee6652ff377b531a</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nasal Cavity">
  <data key="d0">Nasal Cavity</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The upper nasal cavity is a delivery site for dihydroergotamine to improve systemic availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-81fbead48486691cf5945207e3542587</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intranasal Administration">
  <data key="d0">Intranasal Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intranasal administration is a method of delivering dihydroergotamine, including self-administered sprays targeting the upper nasal cavity.&lt;SEP&gt;Intranasal administration is delivered through the nasal route, with triptans administered contralateral to the pain side due to rhinorrhea or nasal congestion ipsilateral to the pain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-81fbead48486691cf5945207e3542587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Antiemetic">
  <data key="d0">Antiemetic</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Antiemetic is a type of drug used to prevent or treat nausea and vomiting, commonly used alongside migraine medications like dihydroergotamine.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-81fbead48486691cf5945207e3542587</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ACHIEVE II Randomized Clinical Trial">
  <data key="d0">ACHIEVE II Randomized Clinical Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The ACHIEVE II Randomized Clinical Trial is a study investigating the effect of ubrogepant versus placebo in the acute treatment of migraine.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c43e57d7c9eb41cc91c89593e5618e6</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="N Engl J Med">
  <data key="d0">N Engl J Med</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">New England Journal of Medicine is a prestigious general medical journal.&lt;SEP&gt;N Engl J Med is a medical journal publishing clinical research on migraine treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c43e57d7c9eb41cc91c89593e5618e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27dde5a0572eb3184020966c72e61c89</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lancet">
  <data key="d0">Lancet</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Lancet is a medical journal publishing clinical research on migraine treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c43e57d7c9eb41cc91c89593e5618e6</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Migraine Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Migraine Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Migraine treatment encompasses various pharmacological and therapeutic approaches for managing acute migraine attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c43e57d7c9eb41cc91c89593e5618e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4041840a72080e115133366da601ba0</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinical Trial">
  <data key="d0">Clinical Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinical trial is a research method used to evaluate the efficacy and safety of triptan therapies, including randomized placebo-controlled trials and meta-analyses.&lt;SEP&gt;Clinical Trial is a research method used to evaluate the safety and efficacy of medical treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c43e57d7c9eb41cc91c89593e5618e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f034fb31d8b9231647be0271fbbe11ff</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711456</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phase 3 Trial">
  <data key="d0">Phase 3 Trial</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Phase 3 Trial refers to the third phase of clinical testing for drug efficacy and safety.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c43e57d7c9eb41cc91c89593e5618e6</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Migraine Medication">
  <data key="d0">Migraine Medication</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Migraine medication includes various drugs such as ubrogepant, rimegepant, zavegepant, and lasmiditan for acute treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c43e57d7c9eb41cc91c89593e5618e6</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Associated Symptom">
  <data key="d0">Associated Symptom</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Associated symptom refers to additional symptoms accompanying the primary pain of migraine.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c43e57d7c9eb41cc91c89593e5618e6</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Valvular Heart Disease">
  <data key="d0">Valvular Heart Disease</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Long-term use of ergotamine may be associated with the development of valvular heart disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-288c1ac0daa4f8d9e6711072456bf290</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cerebrovascular Complications">
  <data key="d0">Cerebrovascular Complications</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Ergotamine overuse is associated with an increased risk of cerebrovascular complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-288c1ac0daa4f8d9e6711072456bf290</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cardiovascular Complications">
  <data key="d0">Cardiovascular Complications</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Ergotamine overuse is associated with an increased risk of cardiovascular complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-288c1ac0daa4f8d9e6711072456bf290</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Peripheral Ischemic Complications">
  <data key="d0">Peripheral Ischemic Complications</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Ergotamine overuse is associated with an increased risk of peripheral ischemic complications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-288c1ac0daa4f8d9e6711072456bf290</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hemiplegic Migraine">
  <data key="d0">Hemiplegic Migraine</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemiplegic migraine is a migraine subtype where ergotamine should be avoided due to the risk of reduced cerebral blood flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-288c1ac0daa4f8d9e6711072456bf290</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Migraine with Prolonged Aura">
  <data key="d0">Migraine with Prolonged Aura</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Migraine with prolonged aura is a contraindication for ergotamine use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-288c1ac0daa4f8d9e6711072456bf290</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dexamethasone">
  <data key="d0">Dexamethasone</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Dexamethasone is a corticosteroid used adjunctively with abortive agents in emergency departments to reduce the risk of early headache recurrence in severe or prolonged migraine.&lt;SEP&gt;Dexamethasone is an adjunctive medication used to reduce the risk of early headache recurrence in emergency department settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Dexamethasone is a treatment compared against sodium valproate in a clinical trial for acute migraine headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Dexamethasone is a glucocorticoid used for initial preventive therapy in patients with infrequent cluster headache attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-288c1ac0daa4f8d9e6711072456bf290&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74803e1d9bd621760a74773f08649443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eced74bbae68c4d04d0938805d606b4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfaea66e0e1b59fcf11083fdc86fa505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e431a39c5b3ac9ad50817fd6694435f0</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711577</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sodium Valproate">
  <data key="d0">Sodium Valproate</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sodium valproate is an anticonvulsant medication that may be effective for acute migraine treatment, particularly when administered intravenously.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium valproate is an alternative option for the treatment of status migrainosus.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium Valproate is a treatment compared against dexamethasone and dopamine antagonists in clinical trials for acute migraine headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium valproate was studied for cluster headache treatment, with mixed results in clinical trials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-288c1ac0daa4f8d9e6711072456bf290&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74803e1d9bd621760a74773f08649443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eced74bbae68c4d04d0938805d606b4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neuromodulation">
  <data key="d0">Neuromodulation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Neuromodulation involves stimulating the central or peripheral nervous system with electrical current or magnetic fields for migraine treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-288c1ac0daa4f8d9e6711072456bf290</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transcutaneous Supraorbital Nerve Stimulation">
  <data key="d0">Transcutaneous Supraorbital Nerve Stimulation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Transcutaneous supraorbital nerve stimulation can reduce migraine pain intensity.&lt;SEP&gt;Transcutaneous supraorbital nerve stimulation is a neuromodulation technique that can reduce migraine pain intensity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-288c1ac0daa4f8d9e6711072456bf290&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c97fa32b2d7b605eb00ea730f0821e9f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Migraine with Brainstem Aura">
  <data key="d0">Migraine with Brainstem Aura</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Migraine with brainstem aura is a contraindication for ergotamine use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-288c1ac0daa4f8d9e6711072456bf290</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711457</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
