<node id="Intravenous Diphenhydramine">
  <data key="d0">Intravenous Diphenhydramine</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5254cc12db8ae366992b8abc63e9bce0</data>
  <data key="d2">Intravenous diphenhydramine is sometimes given with metoclopramide to prevent akathisia and acute dystonic reactions.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Verapamil">
  <data key="d0">Verapamil</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Verapamil is a medication used for prevention of cluster headache and can be used safely with sumatriptan, ergotamine, glucocorticoids, and other preventive agents.&lt;SEP&gt;Verapamil is a prophylactic medication used to treat cluster headache, requiring titration to an effective dose.&lt;SEP&gt;Verapamil is the drug of choice for prophylaxis of episodic and chronic cluster headache; it may be given alone or with a short course of glucocorticoids to help provide rapid suppression of cluster headache attacks during the initial titration.&lt;SEP&gt;Verapamil is recommended as initial preventive therapy for chronic cluster headache and episodic cluster headache with long-lasting active periods.&lt;SEP&gt;Preventive therapy with verapamil rather than other agents for patients with frequent and/or longer cluster periods, typically started at 240 mg daily in three divided doses, with titration up to 960 mg daily as needed.&lt;SEP&gt;Verapamil is a medication used for the prophylaxis of episodic cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697366b5ec6fccd401f60e32f476bcb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e431a39c5b3ac9ad50817fd6694435f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f74beccf3932fc999c5da6217dd983e</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Glucocorticoids">
  <data key="d0">Glucocorticoids</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Glucocorticoids are preventive agents that can be used safely in conjunction with verapamil.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucocorticoids are often used adjunctively with verapamil to provide more rapid benefit during initial titration, or may be used alone as preventive therapy when cluster attacks are infrequent and short.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucocorticoids may be used as adjunctive therapy in the first two weeks of verapamil administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Glucocorticoids are suggested as initial preventive therapy for episodic cluster headache with short active periods and can rapidly suppress attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Short course of glucocorticoids to provide rapid benefit during the initial titration of verapamil, using oral prednisone 100 mg once a day for at least three days followed by tapering.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697366b5ec6fccd401f60e32f476bcb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e431a39c5b3ac9ad50817fd6694435f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f74beccf3932fc999c5da6217dd983e</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Greater occipital nerve block">
  <data key="d0">Greater occipital nerve block</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Greater occipital nerve block is an alternative prophylactic treatment for cluster headache, administered ipsilateral to the headache attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combination therapy">
  <data key="d0">Combination therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combination therapy involves using verapamil in moderate doses (240 to 480 mg daily) with another prophylactic medication such as prednisone, topiramate, or lithium.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prednisone">
  <data key="d0">Prednisone</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Prednisone is a glucocorticoid used for initial preventive therapy in patients with infrequent cluster headache attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Prednisone is a glucocorticoid typically administered as a short course during initial titration of verapamil, often 100 mg once a day for three days followed by tapering.&lt;SEP&gt;Prednisone is a prophylactic medication used in combination with verapamil for cluster headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Oral prednisone 100 mg once a day for at least three days, followed by a taper with a dose reduction of 10 mg every three days.&lt;SEP&gt;Prednisone is a medication studied for short-term prevention of episodic cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697366b5ec6fccd401f60e32f476bcb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e431a39c5b3ac9ad50817fd6694435f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f74beccf3932fc999c5da6217dd983e</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Topiramate">
  <data key="d0">Topiramate</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Topiramate is an add-on medication for cluster headache prevention, often used in combination with verapamil.&lt;SEP&gt;Topiramate is an agent that may be effective as a preventive therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Topiramate is a prophylactic medication used in combination with verapamil for cluster headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Alternative medications such as topiramate for some patients who do not respond to initial preventive therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;Topiramate is a treatment studied for cluster headache prophylaxis in multiple clinical trials and open studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba771d788f7481cea05e87c2e085913d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697366b5ec6fccd401f60e32f476bcb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f74beccf3932fc999c5da6217dd983e</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lithium">
  <data key="d0">Lithium</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Lithium (lithium carbonate) is a medication used for cluster headache prevention, particularly in chronic cases when other drugs are ineffective.&lt;SEP&gt;Lithium is an agent that may be effective as a preventive therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Lithium is a prophylactic medication used in combination with verapamil for cluster headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Alternative medications such as lithium for some patients who do not respond to initial preventive therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;Lithium is a medication compared with verapamil in cluster headache prophylaxis.&lt;SEP&gt;Lithium is a treatment studied for episodic cluster headache in a double-blind placebo-controlled trial from 1997.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba771d788f7481cea05e87c2e085913d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697366b5ec6fccd401f60e32f476bcb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f74beccf3932fc999c5da6217dd983e</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oral ergotamine">
  <data key="d0">Oral ergotamine</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Oral ergotamine has a long half-life and can be used as preventive treatment for nighttime cluster headache attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surgical interventions">
  <data key="d0">Surgical interventions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Surgical interventions are potential treatment options for chronic cluster headache unresponsive to medical treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neurostimulation techniques">
  <data key="d0">Neurostimulation techniques</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Neurostimulation techniques, including sphenopalatine ganglion stimulation and vagus nerve stimulation, are investigational treatments for cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sphenopalatine ganglion stimulation">
  <data key="d0">Sphenopalatine ganglion stimulation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sphenopalatine ganglion stimulation is a neurostimulation technique used for cluster headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Sphenopalatine ganglion stimulation is performed by surgically implanting a neurostimulator that can be activated by the patient using a handheld remote controller; in a trial of 32 patients, it was superior to sham stimulation for pain relief and reduction in attack frequency, though serious adverse events involved lead misplacement and migration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-075c9514b73c9528ed6f8491b449ee40</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vagus nerve stimulation">
  <data key="d0">Vagus nerve stimulation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Vagus nerve stimulation is a neurostimulation technique used for cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Destructive surgical procedures">
  <data key="d0">Destructive surgical procedures</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Destructive surgical procedures are unproven treatments for cluster headache and should be viewed with caution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711568</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Episodic cluster headache">
  <data key="d0">Episodic cluster headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Episodic cluster headache is a type of cluster headache where prophylactic medications should be tapered after the expected duration of the cluster has passed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chronic cluster headache">
  <data key="d0">Chronic cluster headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Chronic cluster headache is a type of cluster headache where a dose reduction trial of preventive medications is suggested every three months if there is a good response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oxygen inhalation">
  <data key="d0">Oxygen inhalation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxygen inhalation is the suggested initial treatment for acute cluster headache attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acute cluster headache">
  <data key="d0">Acute cluster headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acute cluster headache refers to the sudden onset of cluster headache attacks requiring immediate intervention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nonrebreathing facial mask">
  <data key="d0">Nonrebreathing facial mask</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A nonrebreathing facial mask is used to administer oxygen inhalation for acute cluster headache, with a flow rate of at least 12 L/minute.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Demand valve mask">
  <data key="d0">Demand valve mask</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A demand valve mask may enhance the efficacy of oxygen inhalation for acute cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oxygen therapy">
  <data key="d0">Oxygen therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxygen therapy is considered safe and effective for aborting cluster headache attacks, though controlled trial evidence is limited.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mildred">
  <data key="d0">Mildred</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Mildred is not mentioned in the text; this entity was a hallucination from the previous output and should not exist.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypercapnia">
  <data key="d0">Hypercapnia</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypercapnia is a risk for patients with severe chronic obstructive pulmonary disease when treated with inhaled oxygen, potentially leading to CO2 narcosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CO2 narcosis">
  <data key="d0">CO2 narcosis</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">CO2 narcosis is a risk associated with inhaled oxygen in patients with severe chronic obstructive pulmonary disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9064f1ec2a51a8fb5fc12ef54afba305</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pizotifen">
  <data key="d0">Pizotifen</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Pizotifen is an antiserotonergic drug that showed modest improvement in cluster headache in a small crossover trial.&lt;SEP&gt;Pizotifen is an antiserotonergic drug associated with improvement in cluster headache in a single-blind, placebo-controlled, nonrandomized crossover trial of 28 subjects, though it has only a modest effect and is limited by side effects such as tiredness and weight gain.&lt;SEP&gt;Pizotifen (BC-105) is a serotonin antagonist studied for its therapeutic efficacy in vascular headaches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-075c9514b73c9528ed6f8491b449ee40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba771d788f7481cea05e87c2e085913d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Valproate">
  <data key="d0">Valproate</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Valproate (valproic acid) has limited and conflicting evidence for utility in cluster headache prophylaxis; open-label and retrospective studies suggested benefit, but a two-week double-blind randomized controlled trial involving 96 patients found no statistically significant difference between treatment and placebo. It can be used in a dose between 5 and 20 mg/kg daily.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-075c9514b73c9528ed6f8491b449ee40</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capsaicin">
  <data key="d0">Capsaicin</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Capsaicin, applied repeatedly via ipsilateral intranasal application, was reported to be effective in approximately two-thirds of patients with cluster headache in open-label and double-blind, placebo-controlled trials. Its use is uncertain due to induction of pain, sneezing, and nasal secretions.&lt;SEP&gt;Capsaicin is a method involving nasal mucosa application for the treatment of cluster headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Capsaicin is a treatment applied to the nasal mucosa studied for its beneficial effect in cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-075c9514b73c9528ed6f8491b449ee40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e949ceaa91563d5020dfddbce0137142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Melatonin">
  <data key="d0">Melatonin</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Oral melatonin (10 mg) was more effective than placebo in a double-blind, randomized controlled study involving 20 patients, but the response rate was relatively low (5 of 10 patients). Adjunctive melatonin did not produce benefit compared with placebo in a crossover study involving nine patients with refractory cluster headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Melatonin is a method used as adjunctive therapy in the prophylaxis of cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-075c9514b73c9528ed6f8491b449ee40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e949ceaa91563d5020dfddbce0137142</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Botulinum toxin">
  <data key="d0">Botulinum toxin</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Limited, low-quality data suggest that botulinum toxin injections have benefit for some patients with chronic cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-075c9514b73c9528ed6f8491b449ee40</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperbaric oxygen">
  <data key="d0">Hyperbaric oxygen</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A small placebo-controlled, double-blind trial found that hyperbaric oxygen was ineffective in preventing cluster headache attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-075c9514b73c9528ed6f8491b449ee40</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Noninvasive vagus nerve stimulation">
  <data key="d0">Noninvasive vagus nerve stimulation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Noninvasive vagus nerve stimulation may reduce the frequency of cluster headache attacks; however, evidence is inconsistent, with one open-label trial showing significant reductions in attacks per week, while a double-blind randomized trial found no difference between VNS and sham stimulation in achieving pain-free status.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-075c9514b73c9528ed6f8491b449ee40</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deep brain stimulation">
  <data key="d0">Deep brain stimulation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Deep brain stimulation (DBS) of the posterior inferior hypothalamic region is a promising but unproven investigational treatment for intractable cluster headache; in an analysis of 40 patients, DBS was associated with a 77 percent mean reduction of headache frequency among responders, though it carries risks such as intracerebral hemorrhage and requires stringent patient selection criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-075c9514b73c9528ed6f8491b449ee40</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cluster headache">
  <data key="d0">Cluster headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster headache is a medical condition characterized by medically refractory episodes, for which various pharmacological and surgical neurostimulation treatments are explored, with varying degrees of efficacy and safety profiles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-075c9514b73c9528ed6f8491b449ee40</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intracerebral hemorrhage">
  <data key="d0">Intracerebral hemorrhage</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Intracerebral hemorrhage is a rare but life-threatening adverse effect associated with deep brain stimulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-075c9514b73c9528ed6f8491b449ee40</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neurostimulator lead misplacement">
  <data key="d0">Neurostimulator lead misplacement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Neurostimulator lead misplacement is a serious adverse event involving incorrect positioning of the lead during sphenopalatine ganglion stimulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-075c9514b73c9528ed6f8491b449ee40</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neurostimulator lead migration">
  <data key="d0">Neurostimulator lead migration</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Neurostimulator lead migration is a serious adverse event involving the displacement of the lead after sphenopalatine ganglion stimulation implantation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-075c9514b73c9528ed6f8491b449ee40</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711569</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cocaine">
  <data key="d0">Cocaine</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Cocaine is a substance studied in the context of treating cluster headache attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Illicit drug that increases the risk of stroke and intracranial bleeding.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccbcc20d04c05bb1a254eb147d0d3a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711758</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nitroglycerin">
  <data key="d0">Nitroglycerin</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Nitroglycerin is a substance used to induce cluster headache attacks in research.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711570</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ergotamine Tartrate">
  <data key="d0">Ergotamine Tartrate</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Ergotamine tartrate is a medication studied for Horton's histaminic cephalalgia (also known as Harris's ciliary neuralgia).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711570</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Domperidone">
  <data key="d0">Domperidone</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Domperidone is an antiemetic medication commonly administered with DHE to counteract nausea.&lt;SEP&gt;Domperidone is a medication studied for its safety in treating nausea associated with dihydroergotamine infusion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f74beccf3932fc999c5da6217dd983e</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711570</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Octreotide">
  <data key="d0">Octreotide</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Octreotide may be effective in treating acute cluster headaches; in a trial of 57 patients, a single subcutaneous dose (100 mcg) was superior to placebo in cluster headache response at 30 minutes.&lt;SEP&gt;Octreotide is suggested as an alternative agent for patients who do not tolerate or respond to initial therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;Octreotide is a medication studied for prophylactic treatment of cluster headache in a randomized placebo-controlled trial.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f74beccf3932fc999c5da6217dd983e</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711570</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Galcanezumab">
  <data key="d0">Galcanezumab</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Galcanezumab is a human monoclonal antibody that binds to the calcitonin gene-related peptide (CGRP) ligand and is used for the prevention of episodic cluster headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Galcanezumab is an agent that may be effective as a preventive therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Alternative preventive option for patients with prior cluster headache periods lasting longer than one month when first-line preventive medications are ineffective, poorly tolerated, or contraindicated.&lt;SEP&gt;Galcanezumab is a medication studied for the prevention of episodic and chronic cluster headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Galcanezumab is a drug studied in Phase 3 randomized, placebo-controlled trials for chronic cluster headache prevention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697366b5ec6fccd401f60e32f476bcb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e431a39c5b3ac9ad50817fd6694435f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f74beccf3932fc999c5da6217dd983e</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711570</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Methylprednisolone">
  <data key="d0">Methylprednisolone</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Methylprednisolone is a medication studied for prophylactic treatment of episodic cluster headache via intravenous bolus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711570</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trigeminal Autonomic Cephalalgias">
  <data key="d0">Trigeminal Autonomic Cephalalgias</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Trigeminal autonomic cephalalgias (TACs) are a group of idiopathic headache disorders including cluster headache, paroxysmal hemicrania, short-lasting unilateral neuralgiform headache attacks, and hemicrania continua.&lt;SEP&gt;Trigeminal autonomic cephalalgias is a group of primary headache disorders that includes cluster headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Trigeminal autonomic cephalalgias are a group of primary headache syndromes including cluster headache, paroxysmal hemicrania, short-lasting unilateral neuralgiform headache attacks, and hemicrania continua.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711667</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hemicrania Continua">
  <data key="d0">Hemicrania Continua</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemicrania continua is a type of trigeminal autonomic cephalalgia characterized by continuous unilateral headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemicrania continua is a primary headache disorder studied alongside trigeminal autonomic cephalalgias.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711570</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nexon Technologies">
  <data key="d0">Nexon Technologies</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Nexon Technologies is a tech company that saw its stock decline by 7.8% after reporting lower-than-expected quarterly earnings.&lt;SEP&gt;Nexon Technologies is a tech company that saw its stock decline by 7.8% after disappointing earnings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697366b5ec6fccd401f60e32f476bcb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-764b1321ae6bc951a2c8d2de5901567f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Omega Energy">
  <data key="d0">Omega Energy</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Omega Energy is an energy company that gained 2.1% in stock value due to rising oil prices.&lt;SEP&gt;Omega Energy is an energy company that gained 2.1% in stock value due to rising oil prices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-764b1321ae6bc951a2c8d2de5901567f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711754</data>
