<node id="Crude Oil">
  <data key="d0">Crude Oil</data>
  <data key="d1">product</data>
  <data key="d2">Crude oil prices rose to $87.60 per barrel due to supply constraints and strong demand.&lt;SEP&gt;Crude oil prices rose to $87.60 per barrel due to supply constraints and strong demand.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-764b1321ae6bc951a2c8d2de5901567f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cluster Headache">
  <data key="d0">Cluster Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster headache is a primary headache disorder characterized by severe, unilateral pain, typically around the eye, occurring in recurrent cluster periods. It is classified as a trigeminal autonomic cephalalgia, distinguished by intense pain accompanied by ipsilateral cranial autonomic symptoms. The condition is chronic and lifelong, often marked by severe attacks that may gradually decline with increasing age. Despite appropriate treatment, it results in severe functional consequences and significantly impacts quality of life. Cluster headache is further associated with an increased risk of depression and represents a major focus of studied treatments across various modalities.&lt;SEP&gt;Cluster headache is a benign primary headache disorder.&lt;SEP&gt;The large majority of these patients will ultimately be diagnosed with either a migraine or cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bcde2da429cc0d5c293fedea4e0af9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e949ceaa91563d5020dfddbce0137142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697366b5ec6fccd401f60e32f476bcb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f74beccf3932fc999c5da6217dd983e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36b9bf57cb93bcd7302da2d7f4b4041b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-764b1321ae6bc951a2c8d2de5901567f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Market Selloff">
  <data key="d0">Market Selloff</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Market selloff refers to the significant decline in stock values due to investor concerns over interest rates and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Market selloff refers to the significant decline in stock values due to investor concerns over interest rates and regulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697366b5ec6fccd401f60e32f476bcb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-764b1321ae6bc951a2c8d2de5901567f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Federal Reserve Policy Announcement">
  <data key="d0">Federal Reserve Policy Announcement</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Federal Reserve's upcoming policy announcement is expected to impact investor confidence and market stability.&lt;SEP&gt;The Federal Reserve's upcoming policy announcement is expected to impact investor confidence and market stability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697366b5ec6fccd401f60e32f476bcb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-764b1321ae6bc951a2c8d2de5901567f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="3.4% Decline">
  <data key="d0">3.4% Decline</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Global Tech Index experienced a 3.4% decline in midday trading.&lt;SEP&gt;The Global Tech Index experienced a 3.4% decline in midday trading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3bc3f7fc9283c8a89abea7bd6a2953&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-764b1321ae6bc951a2c8d2de5901567f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intranasal Sumatriptan">
  <data key="d0">Intranasal Sumatriptan</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intranasal sumatriptan is a treatment administered through the nasal route, which is more convenient but showed a slower speed of response compared to subcutaneous administration in studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intranasal Zolmitriptan">
  <data key="d0">Intranasal Zolmitriptan</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intranasal zolmitriptan at a dose of 5 or 10 mg was modestly effective at 30 minutes for acute cluster headache compared with placebo in a randomized trial involving 69 patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oral Zolmitriptan">
  <data key="d0">Oral Zolmitriptan</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Oral zolmitriptan 10 mg was modestly effective for acute episodic cluster headache within 30 minutes in a placebo-controlled trial.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dihydroergotamine (DHE)">
  <data key="d0">Dihydroergotamine (DHE)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intravenous dihydroergotamine given in the inpatient or outpatient setting may be effective for cluster headache, administered as a 1 mg intravenous bolus and may be repeated at one hour with a maximum dose of 3 mg in 24 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tachyphylaxis">
  <data key="d0">Tachyphylaxis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tachyphylaxis with recurrent use of triptans seems to be rare in cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Promethazine">
  <data key="d0">Promethazine</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Promethazine is an antiemetic medication commonly administered with DHE to counteract nausea.&lt;SEP&gt;Promethazine is an antiemetic medication that can be administered with dihydroergotamine (DHE) to manage nausea.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f74beccf3932fc999c5da6217dd983e</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trigeminal Denervation">
  <data key="d0">Trigeminal Denervation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Trigeminal denervation is a surgical approach historically used to treat chronic cluster headache, though evidence suggests it may not be effective in preventing headache attacks or autonomic symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sphenopalatine Ganglion Stimulation">
  <data key="d0">Sphenopalatine Ganglion Stimulation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sphenopalatine ganglion stimulation is a therapy found beneficial for a subset of patients with cluster headache in open-label studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Occipital Nerve Stimulation (ONS)">
  <data key="d0">Occipital Nerve Stimulation (ONS)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Occipital nerve stimulation (ONS) involves electronic stimulation of subcutaneous electrodes implanted in the bilateral occipital region via an implanted pulse generator.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gamma Knife Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Gamma Knife Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Gamma knife treatment is a procedure utilized for cluster headache, with outcomes graded as excellent, good, or failure in clinical studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trigeminal Nerve Root Section">
  <data key="d0">Trigeminal Nerve Root Section</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Trigeminal nerve root section involves total or partial section of the trigeminal nerve root and has been associated with complete or near-complete relief of symptoms in a majority of patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trigeminal Sensory Root Section">
  <data key="d0">Trigeminal Sensory Root Section</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Complete surgical section of the trigeminal sensory root is a procedure with reported lack of long-term effect on cluster attack frequency or intensity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Occipital Nerves">
  <data key="d0">Occipital Nerves</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Occipital nerves are targets for newer surgical procedures aimed at treating chronic cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Greater Superficial Petrosal Nerve">
  <data key="d0">Greater Superficial Petrosal Nerve</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The greater superficial petrosal nerve is an autonomic pathway targeted in surgical procedures for cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nervus Intermedius">
  <data key="d0">Nervus Intermedius</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nervus intermedius is an autonomic pathway targeted in surgical procedures for cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trigeminal Ganglion">
  <data key="d0">Trigeminal Ganglion</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The trigeminal ganglion is a target of sensory trigeminal nerve procedures for cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infraorbital Nerve">
  <data key="d0">Infraorbital Nerve</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The infraorbital nerve is a target of sensory trigeminal nerve procedures for cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trigeminal Root">
  <data key="d0">Trigeminal Root</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The trigeminal root is a target of surgical procedures for cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oxygen Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Oxygen Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxygen therapy is used to abort individual attacks of cluster headache but does not reduce the duration of the cluster bout.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxygen therapy is suggested as initial treatment for acute cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neurostimulator Lead">
  <data key="d0">Neurostimulator Lead</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Neurostimulator lead is a device component; misplacement and migration are serious adverse events associated with stimulation therapies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Implanted Pulse Generator">
  <data key="d0">Implanted Pulse Generator</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Implanted pulse generator is a device used in occipital nerve stimulation, delivering electronic stimulation to subcutaneous electrodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Attack Frequency Reduction">
  <data key="d0">Attack Frequency Reduction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reduction in attack frequency was observed as a secondary endpoint in clinical studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Surgical Complications">
  <data key="d0">Surgical Complications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Surgical complications include trigeminal neuralgia, anesthesia dolorosa, hypesthesia, meningitis, and cerebrospinal fluid leak.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Long-term Safety">
  <data key="d0">Long-term Safety</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Long-term safety of device implantation requires additional data to establish, particularly regarding stimulation protocols and patient selection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quality of Life">
  <data key="d0">Quality of Life</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster headache results in marked functional disability and reduced quality of life, even with appropriate treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Depression Risk">
  <data key="d0">Depression Risk</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster headache has been associated with an increased risk of depression.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chronic Cluster Headache">
  <data key="d0">Chronic Cluster Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Chronic cluster headache is defined as continuous headaches or remission intervals of less than 3 months.&lt;SEP&gt;Chronic cluster headache is a severe trigeminal autonomic cephalalgia recognized for its intensity, significantly impacting quality of life and associated with increased risk of depression, and characterized by attacks that may still occur in 80 percent of patients even 15 years after onset.&lt;SEP&gt;Chronic cluster headache is a persistent form of cluster headache studied in clinical descriptive research.&lt;SEP&gt;Chronic cluster headache is a subtype of cluster headache defined by frequent attacks, investigated in preventive treatment studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bcde2da429cc0d5c293fedea4e0af9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697366b5ec6fccd401f60e32f476bcb8</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acute Cluster Headache">
  <data key="d0">Acute Cluster Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">Acute cluster headache refers to headache episodes requiring initial treatment with oxygen or triptans, with alternatives including intranasal lidocaine, oral ergotamine, and intravenous dihydroergotamine.&lt;SEP&gt;Acute cluster headache is the immediate presentation of the condition, for which initial treatment with oxygen or triptans is suggested.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697366b5ec6fccd401f60e32f476bcb8</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Beyond the Basics">
  <data key="d0">Beyond the Basics</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Beyond the Basics are patient education pieces written at the 10th to 12th grade reading level for in-depth information on headache treatment in adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="The Basics">
  <data key="d0">The Basics</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Basics are patient education pieces written in plain language at the 5th to 6th grade reading level answering key patient questions about a given condition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gamma Knife">
  <data key="d0">Gamma Knife</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Gamma knife is a radiosurgery procedure utilized in the treatment of cluster headache, with outcomes graded as excellent, good, or failure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trigeminal Neuralgia">
  <data key="d0">Trigeminal Neuralgia</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Trigeminal neuralgia is a reported complication of destructive surgical procedures used to treat chronic cluster headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Headache suspected to originate from maxillofacial conditions such as temporomandibular joint (TMJ) disorders or trigeminal neuralgia is best evaluated with head MRI without and with IV contrast.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36b9bf57cb93bcd7302da2d7f4b4041b</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711760</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anesthesia Dolorosa">
  <data key="d0">Anesthesia Dolorosa</data>
  <data key="d1">complication</data>
  <data key="d2">Anesthesia dolorosa is a reported complication of destructive surgical procedures used to treat chronic cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypesthesia">
  <data key="d0">Hypesthesia</data>
  <data key="d1">complication</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypesthesia is a reported complication of destructive surgical procedures used to treat chronic cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Meningitis">
  <data key="d0">Meningitis</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Meningitis is a reported complication of destructive surgical procedures used to treat chronic cluster headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Meningitis is an infection that may present with headache and is suggested by meningeal signs on examination.&lt;SEP&gt;Meningitis is inflammation of the meninges, the protective membranes covering the brain and spinal cord.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88449f41c18acfddbc679b10a20feb42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44f11db3bcd7ce2dafa15cd85b96c021</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711755</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cerebrospinal Fluid Leak">
  <data key="d0">Cerebrospinal Fluid Leak</data>
  <data key="d1">complication</data>
  <data key="d2">Cerebrospinal fluid leak is a reported complication of destructive surgical procedures used to treat chronic cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Functional Disability">
  <data key="d0">Functional Disability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster headache results in marked functional disability, even when appropriate treatments are used.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quality of Life Reduction">
  <data key="d0">Quality of Life Reduction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster headache is associated with a reduced quality of life.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suicide Risk">
  <data key="d0">Suicide Risk</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster headache is recognized as so vicious that some patients attempt suicide if the disease is not diagnosed or successfully treated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lifelong Condition">
  <data key="d0">Lifelong Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Limited data suggest that cluster headache is a lifelong condition, although the proportion of patients experiencing attacks gradually declines with increasing age.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Age-Related Decline">
  <data key="d0">Age-Related Decline</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The proportion of patients experiencing cluster headache attacks gradually declines with increasing age.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711572</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="15-Year Prognosis">
  <data key="d0">15-Year Prognosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Even 15 years after cluster headache onset, attacks still occur in 80 percent of patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fcccbfac9c2ef745a159d63b88ddc90</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711573</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eur Neurol">
  <data key="d0">Eur Neurol</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Eur Neurol is a medical journal publication from 1981 reporting on cluster headache cases.</data>
