  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fontaine D">
  <data key="d0">Fontaine D</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Fontaine D is a researcher who published studies on anatomical location of effective deep brain stimulation electrodes in chronic cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e949ceaa91563d5020dfddbce0137142</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lazorthes Y">
  <data key="d0">Lazorthes Y</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lazorthes Y is a researcher who published studies on safety and efficacy of deep brain stimulation in refractory cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e949ceaa91563d5020dfddbce0137142</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Akram H">
  <data key="d0">Akram H</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Akram H is a researcher who published studies on ventral tegmental area deep brain stimulation for refractory chronic cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e949ceaa91563d5020dfddbce0137142</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nowacki A">
  <data key="d0">Nowacki A</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Nowacki A is a researcher who published a meta-analysis of individual patient data on deep brain stimulation for chronic cluster headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Nowacki A is an author of a meta-analysis on Deep Brain Stimulation for Chronic Cluster Headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e949ceaa91563d5020dfddbce0137142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f561f3e1980fae1e2fbac5ed5564517</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Schoenen J">
  <data key="d0">Schoenen J</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Schoenen J is a researcher who published a pilot study on hypothalamic stimulation in chronic cluster headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Schoenen J is an author of a study on sphenopalatine ganglion stimulation for cluster headache treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Schoenen J is an author of a study on hypothalamic stimulation in chronic cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e949ceaa91563d5020dfddbce0137142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f561f3e1980fae1e2fbac5ed5564517</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Botulinum Toxin A">
  <data key="d0">Botulinum Toxin A</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Botulinum Toxin A is a method reviewed according to evidence-based medicine criteria for treatment of headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e949ceaa91563d5020dfddbce0137142</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperbaric Oxygen">
  <data key="d0">Hyperbaric Oxygen</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hyperbaric oxygen is a method involving treatment of active cluster headache in a double-blind placebo-controlled cross-over study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e949ceaa91563d5020dfddbce0137142</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-invasive Vagus Nerve Stimulation">
  <data key="d0">Non-invasive Vagus Nerve Stimulation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Non-invasive vagus nerve stimulation is a method for PREVention and Acute treatment of chronic cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e949ceaa91563d5020dfddbce0137142</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deep Brain Stimulation">
  <data key="d0">Deep Brain Stimulation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Deep brain stimulation is a method explored for refractory cluster hypothalamus or midbrain tegmentum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e949ceaa91563d5020dfddbce0137142</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypothalamic Stimulation">
  <data key="d0">Hypothalamic Stimulation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypothalamic stimulation is a method for intractable cluster headache with long-term experience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e949ceaa91563d5020dfddbce0137142</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OnabotulinumtoxinA">
  <data key="d0">OnabotulinumtoxinA</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">OnabotulinumtoxinA is an artifact involving repeated injections towards the sphenopalatine ganglion in patients with chronic cluster headache and chronic migraine.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e949ceaa91563d5020dfddbce0137142</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inductive Study">
  <data key="d0">Inductive Study</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inductive study refers to a pilot study of efficacy and mode of action in hypothalamic stimulation in chronic cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e949ceaa91563d5020dfddbce0137142</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oxygen">
  <data key="d0">Oxygen</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxygen is recommended as initial acute therapy for cluster headache and is administered without side effects in hospital or emergency settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxygen is suggested as initial treatment for patients with acute cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697366b5ec6fccd401f60e32f476bcb8</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intranasal Triptans">
  <data key="d0">Intranasal Triptans</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intranasal triptans (sumatriptan 20 mg or zolmitriptan 5 mg) are administered contralateral to the side of headache and have a slower onset than subcutaneous injection.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oral Ergotamine">
  <data key="d0">Oral Ergotamine</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Oral ergotamine may be effective for acute cluster headache and has a longer half-life than triptans, allowing use as a short-term preventive treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intravenous Dihydroergotamine">
  <data key="d0">Intravenous Dihydroergotamine</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Intravenous dihydroergotamine may be effective for acute cluster headache based on retrospective data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Greater Occipital Nerve Block">
  <data key="d0">Greater Occipital Nerve Block</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Greater occipital nerve block ipsilateral to headache attacks is an alternative preventive therapy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paroxysmal Hemicrania">
  <data key="d0">Paroxysmal Hemicrania</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Paroxysmal hemicrania is a type of trigeminal autonomic cephalalgia characterized by recurrent attacks of unilateral pain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Short-Lasting Unilateral Neuralgiform Headache Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Short-Lasting Unilateral Neuralgiform Headache Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Short-lasting unilateral neuralgiform headache attacks are a type of trigeminal autonomic cephalalgia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Triptan Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Triptan Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Triptan therapy is used to abort individual attacks of cluster headache but does not reduce the duration of the cluster bout.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Preventive Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Preventive Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Preventive therapy aims to suppress attacks over the expected duration of the cluster period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acute Therapy">
  <data key="d0">Acute Therapy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Acute therapy is useful for aborting individual attacks of cluster headache but does not reduce the duration of the cluster headache bout.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cluster Period">
  <data key="d0">Cluster Period</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The cluster period is the duration of recurrent attacks, typically lasting weeks or longer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Treatment Guidelines">
  <data key="d0">Treatment Guidelines</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Treatment guidelines recommend initial therapy with oxygen or triptans for acute cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Richard P Goddeau, Jr, DO, FAHA">
  <data key="d0">Richard P Goddeau, Jr, DO, FAHA</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Richard P Goddeau, Jr, DO, FAHA is a Deputy Editor of the article on cluster headache treatment and prognosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Jerry W Swanson, MD, MHPE">
  <data key="d0">Jerry W Swanson, MD, MHPE</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Jerry W Swanson, MD, MHPE is a Section Editor of the article on cluster headache treatment and prognosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Arne May, MD">
  <data key="d0">Arne May, MD</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Arne May, MD is the Author of the article on cluster headache treatment and prognosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-604091b1b25ec431b6eb74ffe266e830</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="United States Food and Drug Administration">
  <data key="d0">United States Food and Drug Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The United States Food and Drug Administration issued a headache-related approval in 2019.&lt;SEP&gt;The United States Food and Drug Administration approved galcanezumab for preventive treatment of episodic cluster headache in 2019.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba771d788f7481cea05e87c2e085913d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e431a39c5b3ac9ad50817fd6694435f0</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fremanezumab">
  <data key="d0">Fremanezumab</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Fremanezumab is a CGRP antibody reported to reduce cluster headache attacks in patients with comorbid migraine.&lt;SEP&gt;Fremanezumab is a CGRP antibody with limited and conflicted data for the prevention of cluster headaches.&lt;SEP&gt;Fremanezumab is a drug studied for comorbid cluster headache in patients with migraine and for the prevention of episodic and chronic cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba771d788f7481cea05e87c2e085913d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e431a39c5b3ac9ad50817fd6694435f0</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eptinezumab">
  <data key="d0">Eptinezumab</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Eptinezumab is a CGRP antibody assessed in an open-label study for chronic cluster headache prevention.&lt;SEP&gt;Eptinezumab is a drug studied for long-term safety, tolerability, and efficacy in chronic cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba771d788f7481cea05e87c2e085913d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Greater Occipital Nerve Blockade">
  <data key="d0">Greater Occipital Nerve Blockade</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Greater occipital nerve blockade is a therapeutic method studied for cluster headache, including steroid injections and nerve blocks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Episodic Cluster Headache">
  <data key="d0">Episodic Cluster Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Episodic cluster headache is characterized by active cluster periods that are infrequent and last less than four weeks.&lt;SEP&gt;Episodic cluster headache is a subtype of cluster headache with periodic occurrences, investigated in preventive treatment studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697366b5ec6fccd401f60e32f476bcb8</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="US FDA">
  <data key="d0">US FDA</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">US FDA is the regulatory body that provided labeling information for galcanezumab.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinical Trials">
  <data key="d0">Clinical Trials</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinical trials are research studies evaluating the efficacy and safety of treatments such as galcanezumab, fremanezumab, and eptinezumab for cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-feb1965a69687b7da4c479723318f38b</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Schober M">
  <data key="d0">Schober M</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Schober M is an author of a meta-analysis on Deep Brain Stimulation for Chronic Cluster Headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f561f3e1980fae1e2fbac5ed5564517</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nader L">
  <data key="d0">Nader L</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Nader L is an author of a meta-analysis on Deep Brain Stimulation for Chronic Cluster Headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f561f3e1980fae1e2fbac5ed5564517</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deep Brain Stimulation for Chronic Cluster Headache: Meta-Analysis of Individual Patient Data">
  <data key="d0">Deep Brain Stimulation for Chronic Cluster Headache: Meta-Analysis of Individual Patient Data</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Deep Brain Stimulation for Chronic Cluster Headache: Meta-Analysis of Individual Patient Data is a study analyzing individual patient data on the efficacy of deep brain stimulation for chronic cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f561f3e1980fae1e2fbac5ed5564517</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypothalamic stimulation in chronic cluster headache">
  <data key="d0">Hypothalamic stimulation in chronic cluster headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypothalamic stimulation in chronic cluster headache is a study investigating the efficacy and mode of action of hypothalamic stimulation for chronic cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f561f3e1980fae1e2fbac5ed5564517</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deep brain stimulation for intractable chronic cluster headache">
  <data key="d0">Deep brain stimulation for intractable chronic cluster headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Deep brain stimulation for intractable chronic cluster headache is a study proposing patient selection criteria for deep brain stimulation in intractable chronic cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f561f3e1980fae1e2fbac5ed5564517</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Jürgens TP">
  <data key="d0">Jürgens TP</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Jürgens TP is an author of a study on long-term effectiveness of sphenopalatine ganglion stimulation for cluster headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Jürgens TP is an author of a study on sphenopalatine ganglion stimulation in intractable cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f561f3e1980fae1e2fbac5ed5564517</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stimulation of the sphenopalatine ganglion in intractable cluster headache">
  <data key="d0">Stimulation of the sphenopalatine ganglion in intractable cluster headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stimulation of the sphenopalatine ganglion in intractable cluster headache is an expert consensus on patient selection and standards of care.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f561f3e1980fae1e2fbac5ed5564517</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711576</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stimulation of the sphenopalatine ganglion (SPG) for cluster headache treatment">
  <data key="d0">Stimulation of the sphenopalatine ganglion (SPG) for cluster headache treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stimulation of the sphenopalatine ganglion (SPG) for cluster headache treatment is a randomized, sham-controlled study (Pathway CH-1).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f561f3e1980fae1e2fbac5ed5564517</data>
