</node>
<node id="Subarachnoid Hemorrhage">
  <data key="d0">Subarachnoid Hemorrhage</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Subarachnoid hemorrhage (SAH) is a type of intracranial hemorrhage involving bleeding into the subarachnoid space.&lt;SEP&gt;Subarachnoid hemorrhage is a lifethreatening condition requiring urgent diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Subarachnoid hemorrhage is a serious secondary cause of thunderclap headache, occurring in approximately 8 percent of emergency department patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Subarachnoid hemorrhage (SAH) is a type of stroke that can present with sudden "thunderclap" headaches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88449f41c18acfddbc679b10a20feb42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d93c3ae2e3eb96980253ed880c4042a8</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbon Monoxide Poisoning">
  <data key="d0">Carbon Monoxide Poisoning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbon monoxide (CO) poisoning is a cause of nontraumatic headache resulting from inhalation of carbon monoxide.&lt;SEP&gt;Toxic exposure – Headaches that involve multiple family members or coworkers and improve rapidly in the emergency department (ED) without intervention, particularly during winter months, raise the possibility of carbon monoxide poisoning.&lt;SEP&gt;Simultaneous headaches in multiple family members suggest carbon monoxide poisoning.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon monoxide poisoning is a medical condition identified by symptoms such as headache and exposure to enclosed spaces with sources like gasoline or kerosene generators.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62c387dc1abd6c2085428bd5bab9c2b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccbcc20d04c05bb1a254eb147d0d3a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711752</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intracranial Hemorrhage">
  <data key="d0">Intracranial Hemorrhage</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Intracranial hemorrhage (ICH) refers to bleeding within the brain tissue or surrounding spaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Intracranial hemorrhage is a lifethreatening condition requiring urgent diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Intracranial hemorrhage is bleeding within the skull, often described as the "first" and "worst headache of my life".</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88449f41c18acfddbc679b10a20feb42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccbcc20d04c05bb1a254eb147d0d3a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF&lt;SEP&gt;iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cerebral Venous Thrombosis">
  <data key="d0">Cerebral Venous Thrombosis</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Cerebral venous thrombosis (CVT) is a cause of headache resulting from thrombosis of the cerebral venous sinuses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711667</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Human Immunodeficiency Virus">
  <data key="d0">Human Immunodeficiency Virus</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) is a viral infection that can be associated with secondary headache syndromes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711667</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tension-Type Headache">
  <data key="d0">Tension-Type Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tension-type headache is a primary headache syndrome characterized by bilateral, pressing/tightening pain of mild to moderate intensity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711667</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="New Persistent Daily Headache">
  <data key="d0">New Persistent Daily Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">New persistent daily headache is a less common primary headache disorder characterized by daily headaches lasting for more than three months.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711667</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Primary Cough Headache">
  <data key="d0">Primary Cough Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Primary cough headache is a less common primary headache disorder triggered by coughing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711667</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Primary Exercise Headache">
  <data key="d0">Primary Exercise Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Primary exercise headache is a less common primary headache disorder triggered by physical exertion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711667</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="New Onset Nontraumatic Headache">
  <data key="d0">New Onset Nontraumatic Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">New onset nontraumatic headache is a clinical presentation involving the assessment of secondary causes (structural, inflammatory) and primary headache syndromes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711667</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Structural Causes">
  <data key="d0">Structural Causes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Structural causes refer to physical abnormalities or lesions identified during the evaluation of nontraumatic headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711667</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inflammatory Causes">
  <data key="d0">Inflammatory Causes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inflammatory causes refer to disease processes involving inflammation identified during the evaluation of nontraumatic headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711667</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Primary Headache Syndromes">
  <data key="d0">Primary Headache Syndromes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Primary headache syndromes are headache disorders not attributable to another medical condition, including migraine, tension-type, and trigeminal autonomic cephalalgias.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711667</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Secondary Headache Syndromes">
  <data key="d0">Secondary Headache Syndromes</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01</data>
  <data key="d2">Human immunodeficiency virus can be associated with secondary headache syndromes.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711667</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Secondary Causes">
  <data key="d0">Secondary Causes</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01</data>
  <data key="d2">The evaluation of new-onset nontraumatic headache involves assessing for secondary causes such as structural and inflammatory conditions.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711667</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
