  <data key="d0">Richard Goddeau</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Richard P Goddeau Jr is a deputy editor contributing to the evaluation of adult nontraumatic headache in the emergency department.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711750</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nontraumatic Headache">
  <data key="d0">Nontraumatic Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nontraumatic headache is the primary clinical presentation, constituting approximately 2 percent of emergency department visits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711750</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Secondary Headache">
  <data key="d0">Secondary Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Secondary headache refers to headaches caused by underlying serious conditions, distinct from benign primary headaches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711750</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Primary Headache">
  <data key="d0">Primary Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Primary headache refers to benign intrinsic causes such as migraine, tension, or cluster headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711750</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thunderclap Headache">
  <data key="d0">Thunderclap Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Thunderclap headache is defined as a severe headache reaching maximal intensity within seconds or minutes, warranting aggressive investigation.&lt;SEP&gt;Thunderclap headache is a severe headache of sudden onset, reaching maximal intensity within seconds or less than one minute.&lt;SEP&gt;Overview of thunderclap headache, section on 'Colloid cyst of the third ventricle'.&lt;SEP&gt;Thunderclap headache is a severe symptom associated with arterial dissection, present in 3.2 percent of carotid dissection and 9 percent of vertebral dissection cases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62c387dc1abd6c2085428bd5bab9c2b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d93c3ae2e3eb96980253ed880c4042a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccbcc20d04c05bb1a254eb147d0d3a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711750</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reversible Cerebral Vasoconstriction Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Reversible Cerebral Vasoconstriction Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reversible cerebral vasoconstriction syndrome is a serious etiology of sudden-onset headache often triggered by vasoactive medications or environmental factors.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carotid and Vertebral Artery Dissections">
  <data key="d0">Carotid and Vertebral Artery Dissections</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Carotid and vertebral artery dissections are serious causes of headache that may present with gradual onset.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Venous Sinus Thrombosis">
  <data key="d0">Venous Sinus Thrombosis</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Venous sinus thrombosis is a serious cause of headache that may present with gradual onset.&lt;SEP&gt;Venous sinus thrombosis is a blood clot in the dural venous sinuses that can present with headaches.&lt;SEP&gt;Venous sinus thrombosis is most common postpartum and can cause headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Venous sinus thrombosis is a less common etiology in pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88449f41c18acfddbc679b10a20feb42</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pituitary Apoplexy">
  <data key="d0">Pituitary Apoplexy</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Pituitary apoplexy is a serious cause of sudden-onset headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Pituitary apoplexy is a less common pregnancy-related etiology of headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Pituitary apoplexy is a less common cause of headache in the pregnant or postpartum patient.&lt;SEP&gt;Pituitary apoplexy is a less common cause of headache in pregnancy and postpartum period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b923e6b3f5a46729e0154937dbba3c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88449f41c18acfddbc679b10a20feb42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36b9bf57cb93bcd7302da2d7f4b4041b</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acute Angle-Closure Glaucoma">
  <data key="d0">Acute Angle-Closure Glaucoma</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acute angle-closure glaucoma is a serious cause of headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Acute angle-closure glaucoma presents with headache, sometimes preceding visual changes or eye pain.&lt;SEP&gt;Acute angle-closure glaucoma patients may present with headache as a primary complaint.&lt;SEP&gt;Acute angle-closure glaucoma is a secondary headache commonly centered around the involved eye.&lt;SEP&gt;Acute angle-closure glaucoma is a sight-threatening emergency characterized by acute headache, eye pain, and diminished vision, typically unilateral.&lt;SEP&gt;Acute angle-closure glaucoma could indicate headache with visual impairment, periorbital pain, or ophthalmoplegia.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62c387dc1abd6c2085428bd5bab9c2b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88449f41c18acfddbc679b10a20feb42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccbcc20d04c05bb1a254eb147d0d3a3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36b9bf57cb93bcd7302da2d7f4b4041b</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unruptured Cerebral Aneurysms">
  <data key="d0">Unruptured Cerebral Aneurysms</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Unruptured cerebral aneurysms are serious causes of headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Colloid Cyst of the Third Ventricle">
  <data key="d0">Colloid Cyst of the Third Ventricle</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Colloid cyst of the third ventricle is a serious cause of headache.&lt;SEP&gt;Postural or positional headache raises concern for spontaneous intracranial hypotension or colloid cyst of the third ventricle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccbcc20d04c05bb1a254eb147d0d3a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypertensive Emergencies">
  <data key="d0">Hypertensive Emergencies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypertensive emergencies are serious causes of headache.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Herpetic Meningitis">
  <data key="d0">Herpetic Meningitis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Herpetic meningitis is a dangerous cause of headache that can present with gradual onset.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lyme Meningitis">
  <data key="d0">Lyme Meningitis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lyme meningitis is a dangerous cause of headache that can present with gradual onset.&lt;SEP&gt;Recent rash compatible with erythema migrans (picture 1) suggests Lyme meningitis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccbcc20d04c05bb1a254eb147d0d3a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brain Tumor">
  <data key="d0">Brain Tumor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Brain tumor is a dangerous cause of headache that can present with gradual onset.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brain Abscess">
  <data key="d0">Brain Abscess</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Brain abscess is a dangerous cause of headache that can present with gradual onset.&lt;SEP&gt;If the drugs are used intravenously (IV), brain abscess is another possibility, even in the absence of fever.&lt;SEP&gt;Brain abscess is a localized collection of pus within the brain tissue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88449f41c18acfddbc679b10a20feb42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccbcc20d04c05bb1a254eb147d0d3a3f</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hypertensive Encephalopathy">
  <data key="d0">Hypertensive Encephalopathy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hypertensive encephalopathy is a dangerous cause of headache that can present with gradual onset.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Posterior Reversible Encephalopathy Syndrome">
  <data key="d0">Posterior Reversible Encephalopathy Syndrome</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Posterior reversible encephalopathy syndrome is a dangerous cause of headache that can present with gradual onset.&lt;SEP&gt;Posterior reversible encephalopathy syndrome is a less common cause of headache in the pregnant or postpartum patient.&lt;SEP&gt;Posterior reversible encephalopathy syndrome (PRES) is a less common cause of headache in pregnancy and postpartum period.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b923e6b3f5a46729e0154937dbba3c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36b9bf57cb93bcd7302da2d7f4b4041b</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Idiopathic Intracranial Hypertension">
  <data key="d0">Idiopathic Intracranial Hypertension</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Idiopathic intracranial hypertension is a dangerous cause of headache that can present with gradual onset.&lt;SEP&gt;Idiopathic intracranial hypertension (pseudotumor cerebri) is a condition characterized by increased intracranial pressure without a clear cause.&lt;SEP&gt;Idiopathic intracranial hypertension can present with headache and visual disturbances.&lt;SEP&gt;Idiopathic intracranial hypertension is a condition most of whom will have papilledema, requiring lumbar puncture with opening pressure measurement for evaluation, but it should follow brain imaging.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62c387dc1abd6c2085428bd5bab9c2b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88449f41c18acfddbc679b10a20feb42</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tension Headache">
  <data key="d0">Tension Headache</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tension headache is a benign primary headache disorder.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intracranial Epidural Hematoma">
  <data key="d0">Intracranial Epidural Hematoma</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intracranial epidural hematoma is a lifethreatening condition requiring urgent diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Central Nervous System Infection">
  <data key="d0">Central Nervous System Infection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Central nervous system infection is a lifethreatening condition requiring urgent diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62</data>
  <data key="d4">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d5">1792711751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acute Bacterial Meningitis">
  <data key="d0">Acute Bacterial Meningitis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acute bacterial meningitis is a central nervous system infection.&lt;SEP&gt;Clinical features and diagnosis of acute bacterial meningitis in adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccbcc20d04c05bb1a254eb147d0d3a3f</data>
