<edge source="Haloperidol" target="Metoclopramide">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Haloperidol and metoclopramide were compared for acute migraine treatment in the emergency department; no difference in pain relief but higher incidence of restlessness (akathisia) with haloperidol.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effects,treatment comparison</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d38115148b4b0478b2ff0c5f850bbcb7</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711465</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Haloperidol" target="Akathisia">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Adverse effects, mainly sedation and akathisia, occurred in 80 percent of patients who received haloperidol.</data>
  <data key="d9">adverse effect association,treatment-related risk</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d38115148b4b0478b2ff0c5f850bbcb7</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711465</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Haloperidol" target="Migraine">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Haloperidol was found effective for migraine pain relief in a placebo-controlled trial.</data>
