</edge>
<edge source="CGRP Antagonists" target="Triptans">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">For patients who do not respond or have a contraindication to triptans, a CGRP antagonist is used.&lt;SEP&gt;Rimegepant has been found to be effective in some patients who did not respond previously to a triptan.</data>
  <data key="d9">migraine therapy,patient eligibility,treatment alternatives,treatment comparison</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d38115148b4b0478b2ff0c5f850bbcb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711466</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="CGRP Antagonists" target="Coronary Artery Disease">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">CGRP antagonists are often used for patients with contraindication (e.g., coronary artery disease) to treatment with triptans and/or antiemetics.</data>
  <data key="d9">contraindication,treatment eligibility</data>
