</edge>
<edge source="Dihydroergotamine" target="Migraine">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Dihydroergotamine is effective for acute migraine, particularly in chronic intractable cases.&lt;SEP&gt;Intranasal dihydroergotamine is efficacious for migraine symptoms with resolution rates of 27 percent within 30 minutes and 70 percent within four hours.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcutaneous dihydroergotamine was more likely to produce relief by 24 hours and associated with lower recurrence compared to sumatriptan.&lt;SEP&gt;Intravenous dihydroergotamine is used for the treatment of chronic intractable migraine headache or status migrainosus.&lt;SEP&gt;Dihydroergotamine is evaluated for acute migraine headache in systematic reviews.</data>
  <data key="d9">acute migraine treatment,efficacy,parenteral use,severity,systematic review,treatment efficacy,treatment method</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-81f90692986dfb1f830a27d0b7536f61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81fbead48486691cf5945207e3542587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c43e57d7c9eb41cc91c89593e5618e6</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711468</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Dihydroergotamine" target="Ergotamine">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Both ergotamine and dihydroergotamine bind to 5HT 1b/d receptors, but dihydroergotamine is a more potent venoconstrictor and has fewer side effects.</data>
  <data key="d9">receptor binding,vasoconstriction</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-81f90692986dfb1f830a27d0b7536f61</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711468</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Dihydroergotamine" target="Triptans">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Alternative options include dihydroergotamine for patients who do not respond to triptans.</data>
  <data key="d9">migraine therapy,treatment alternatives</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711468</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Dihydroergotamine" target="Intravenous Administration">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Intravenous dihydroergotamine is typically administered in combination with an antiemetic drug.</data>
  <data key="d9">administration method,combination therapy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-81fbead48486691cf5945207e3542587</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711470</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Dihydroergotamine" target="Intranasal Administration">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Intranasal dihydroergotamine has been found efficacious in placebo-controlled trials for migraine symptoms.</data>
  <data key="d9">administration method,efficacy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-81fbead48486691cf5945207e3542587</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711470</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Dihydroergotamine" target="Subcutaneous Administration">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Subcutaneous dihydroergotamine may be slightly more effective than intranasal preparation but requires patient self-injection.</data>
  <data key="d9">administration method,efficacy comparison</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-81fbead48486691cf5945207e3542587</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711470</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Dihydroergotamine" target="Antiemetic">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The use of dihydroergotamine is often combined with an antiemetic, and this is always required for intravenous administration.</data>
  <data key="d9">combination therapy,efficacy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-81fbead48486691cf5945207e3542587</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711470</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Dihydroergotamine" target="Verapamil">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
