  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Triptans" target="Intranasal Administration">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Intranasal triptans are administered contralateral to the pain side because patients often have rhinorrhea or nasal congestion ipsilateral to the pain.</data>
  <data key="d9">administration route,pain side consideration</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD - Uptodate - Cluster headache_ Treatment and prognosis.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711580</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Triptans" target="Cardiovascular Risks">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Triptans should be avoided in patients with ischemic cardiovascular disease or stroke, Prinzmetal angina, or uncontrolled arterial hypertension.</data>
  <data key="d9">contraindications,patient safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-f8aa2f95b44d688508b19c8d0fcbc4f3</data>
