</edge>
<edge source="Mild Migraine Attacks" target="Migraine-Specific Agents">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Migraine-specific agents (eg, triptans, CGRP antagonists, lasmiditan, dihydroergotamine) are used for patients with more severe migraine and in those whose headaches respond poorly to NSAIDs or combination analgesics.</data>
  <data key="d9">severity-based,treatment hierarchy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711469</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Moderate to Severe Migraine Attacks" target="Triptan with or without NSAID">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">For moderate to severe migraine attacks not associated with vomiting or severe nausea, first-line oral options include a triptan with or without an NSAID.</data>
  <data key="d9">first-line treatment,moderate to severe attacks</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711468</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Moderate to Severe Migraine Attacks" target="Nonoral Route">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Select a nonoral route of administration for patients whose migraine attacks present early with significant nausea or vomiting.</data>
  <data key="d9">administration route,patient symptoms</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711469</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Moderate to Severe Migraine Attacks" target="Rescue Medication">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Consider a self-administered rescue medication for patients with severe migraine attacks that do not respond well to other treatments.</data>
  <data key="d9">severe attacks,treatment option</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-2878ee960479fec5e0fd7c97d6d44f85</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD - Uptodate - Acute treatment of migraine in adults(1).PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711469</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Medication Overuse Headache" target="Acute Migraine Medications">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Guard against medication overuse headache by educating patients about risk and using preventive medications in patients with frequent headaches.</data>
  <data key="d9">frequent headaches,risk</data>
