<edge source="Subarachnoid Hemorrhage" target="Intracranial Hemorrhage">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Subarachnoid hemorrhage is a specific type of intracranial hemorrhage.</data>
  <data key="d9">hemorrhage type,intracranial bleeding</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711667</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subarachnoid Hemorrhage" target="Sudden-Onset Headache">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Sudden-onset headache reaching maximal intensity within seconds or minutes warrants investigation for subarachnoid hemorrhage.</data>
  <data key="d9">headache type,serious condition</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-7d7e2a1fa6fae352f798fe0d6e8e0e62</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711763</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subarachnoid Hemorrhage" target="Lumbar Puncture">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Lumbar puncture is performed in all patients with suspected subarachnoid hemorrhage when the CT is normal to identify hemorrhage.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic procedure,hemorrhage detection</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d93c3ae2e3eb96980253ed880c4042a8</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711768</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Subarachnoid Hemorrhage" target="Thunderclap Headache">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Approximately 8 percent of emergency department patients with thunderclap headache have a subarachnoid hemorrhage, requiring urgent diagnostic evaluation.</data>
  <data key="d9">cause identification,emergency diagnosis</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d93c3ae2e3eb96980253ed880c4042a8</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711769</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Carbon Monoxide Poisoning" target="Intracranial Hemorrhage">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Carbon monoxide poisoning is a cause of nontraumatic headache, which must be differentiated from intracranial hemorrhage.</data>
  <data key="d9">cause,nontraumatic headache</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711668</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Carbon Monoxide Poisoning" target="Carboxyhemoglobin Concentration">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The diagnosis of carbon monoxide poisoning is confirmed by measuring carboxyhemoglobin concentration with cooximetry.</data>
  <data key="d9">confirmation,diagnostic data</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-62c387dc1abd6c2085428bd5bab9c2b4</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711763</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Carbon Monoxide Poisoning" target="Toxic Exposure">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Headaches that involve multiple family members or coworkers and improve rapidly in the emergency department (ED) without intervention, particularly during winter months, raise the possibility of carbon monoxide poisoning.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnosis,environmental hazard</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ccbcc20d04c05bb1a254eb147d0d3a3f</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711771</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Intracranial Hemorrhage" target="Cerebral Venous Thrombosis">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Cerebral venous thrombosis is a venous cause of headache that must be differentiated from intracranial hemorrhage.</data>
  <data key="d9">cause,venous sinus thrombosis</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-469ba9f85eff0d1ef2fc5b0807c28e01</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Emergency_evaluation_of_the_adult_with_new_nontraumatic.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711668</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Intracranial Hemorrhage" target="CNS Infection">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Descriptions of "first" and "worst headache of my life" sometimes accompany intracranial hemorrhage or CNS infection.</data>
  <data key="d9">"first and worst headache",critical presentation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-88449f41c18acfddbc679b10a20feb42</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711766</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Intracranial Hemorrhage" target="Warfarin">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Patients on warfarin have a higher risk of intracranial hemorrhage compared with those on direct oral anticoagulants (DOACs).</data>
  <data key="d9">bleeding risk,medication comparison</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ccbcc20d04c05bb1a254eb147d0d3a3f</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711771</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Intracranial Hemorrhage" target="Direct Oral Anticoagulants">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Patients on any oral anticoagulant plus antiplatelet agents have an increased risk compared with those not on these agents.</data>
  <data key="d9">bleeding risk,medication comparison</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-ccbcc20d04c05bb1a254eb147d0d3a3f</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711771</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Human Immunodeficiency Virus" target="Secondary Headache Syndromes">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Human immunodeficiency virus can be associated with secondary headache syndromes.</data>
  <data key="d9">medical condition,viral association</data>
