<edge source="Cerebrovascular imaging" target="Diagnostic resolution">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Cerebrovascular imaging is recommended to resolve ambiguity in suspected SAH when suspicion remains after initial evaluation.</data>
  <data key="d9">ambiguity resolution,diagnostic strategy</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d3b99ec17053435d72311359e33c6696</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711772</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Cerebrovascular imaging" target="Lumbar puncture">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">In cases where suspicion for SAH remains, cerebrovascular imaging is recommended to resolve the ambiguity.</data>
  <data key="d9">diagnostic sequence,follow-up</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d3b99ec17053435d72311359e33c6696</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711773</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lumbar puncture" target="Prior CT requirement">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Lumbar puncture should not be delayed to await a head CT in the absence of specific criteria; in their absence, LP can proceed.</data>
  <data key="d9">contraindication,safety protocol</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d3b99ec17053435d72311359e33c6696</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711773</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Lumbar puncture" target="Herniation">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Rare documented cases of herniation following LP have made some clinicians reluctant to perform the procedure without prior imaging.</data>
  <data key="d9">complication risk,procedural safety</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d3b99ec17053435d72311359e33c6696</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
