</edge>
<edge source="Increased Intracranial Pressure" target="Focal Neurologic Deficit">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Focal neurologic deficit is a clinical sign that should suspect increased intracranial pressure when accompanied by headache.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical sign,increased ICP indicator</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-62c387dc1abd6c2085428bd5bab9c2b4</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711765</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Increased Intracranial Pressure" target="Repeated Nausea and Vomiting">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Repeated episodes of nausea and vomiting without another explanation should suspect increased intracranial pressure when accompanied by headache.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical sign,increased ICP indicator</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-62c387dc1abd6c2085428bd5bab9c2b4</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711765</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Suspected acute angle-closure glaucoma" target="Elevated Intraocular Pressure">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Elevated intraocular pressure confirms the diagnosis, and unnecessary neurologic workup and imaging should be avoided to not delay treatment.</data>
  <data key="d9">clinical urgency,diagnostic confirmation</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-62c387dc1abd6c2085428bd5bab9c2b4</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711764</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Infection (Extracranial)" target="Intracranial Abscess">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Infection in an extracranial location such as paranasal or mastoid sinuses, pharynx, or inner ear may serve as a nidus for the development of meningitis or intracranial abscess.</data>
  <data key="d9">infection spread,nidus for development</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-88449f41c18acfddbc679b10a20feb42</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711766</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Headache with Seizure" target="Intracranial Pathology">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Headache associated with seizure is also concerning for intracranial pathology.</data>
  <data key="d9">intracranial concern,seizure association</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-88449f41c18acfddbc679b10a20feb42</data>
  <data key="d11">iMD_Uptodate_Evaluation_of_the_adult_with_nontraumatic_headache.PDF</data>
  <data key="d12">1792711766</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
</graph></graphml>